  "notes": "**Fix: the update card shows its Install button.** Up to 0.2.3, the card that offers a new version showed text like `[object HTMLParagraphElement]` instead of **Install and restart** and **Later**. The port route window and the Diagnostics header had the same fault and are fixed too.\n\n**Install this version by hand.** The fix only works once it's installed, so your current version can't show the button for this update:\n1. Close Aether DV. If you started an engine yourself, stop it too.\n2. From this release, download the installer of the same type you used before: `\u2026_x64-setup.exe` or `\u2026_x64_en-US.msi` on Windows, `.dmg` on macOS, or your usual Linux package.\n3. Run it. Settings, configuration files and recordings are kept.\n\nFrom 0.2.4 on, updates install from the button again.\n\nAlso:\n- **Radio test summary:** \"Messages waited, by reason\" now counts only time when a message was actually waiting. It used to add up every busy period, even with nothing to send.\n- **Credits:** Diagnostics has a new **About** section, crediting D-RATS and the people who built and maintain it. Aether DV speaks the D-RATS protocol.\n\nStill **tested on the bench only**: two radios on simplex, no repeaters or D-RATS stations yet.",
